+The experiment must expose the uncertain dimension itself. Size and fidelity follow
+the uncertainty; a cheaper artifact that substitutes another dimension is not proof.
+
+## Prove the outcome
+
+Derive the affected public surfaces and complete user journeys from the change. Account
+for each as passed, failed, or untested with a reason. An observed failure remains a
+failure until a completed retest replaces it; untested or unanswered work is unknown,
+not pass.
+
+For a measurable optimization, record the baseline, change one causal hypothesis at a
+time, reject an obvious loser with the cheapest discriminating check, and run the full
+proof before keeping a winner.
+
+For a resumable workflow with external side effects, make each transition idempotent.
+Confirm the effect and durably record it before advancing progress.
+
